The@propertyrule is used to define custom 
CSS properties (CSS variables) directly in the stylesheet without having to run any 
JavaScript.

The@propertyrule has data type checking 
and constraining, sets a default value, and specifies the inherit behaviour.

The definition below creates a custom property named --myColor, defines it as a color property, 
specifies that it will inherit values from its parent elements, and its default value is lightgray.

The CSSvar()function is used to insert the custom property in CSS:

